{"id":"leetcode-99","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Recover Binary Search Tree","summary":"Given the root of a binary search tree where exactly two nodes have incorrect values, correct the tree by swapping the values of these nodes without altering the tree's structure.","statement":"Given the root of a binary search tree where exactly two nodes have incorrect values, correct the tree by swapping the values of these nodes without altering the tree's structure.","constraints":["2 <= node count <= 1000; -2^31 <= Node.val <= 2^31−1.","All node values are distinct. Exactly two values were swapped in an otherwise valid BST.","Modify the original values without changing the final left/right links or replacing nodes; return None.","An O(n)-space solution is allowed. Follow-up: O(1) auxiliary space; temporary traversal links must be restored."],"topics":["trees","binary-search-trees","inorder-traversal"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"recover_bst","parameters":[{"name":"root","annotation":"TreeNode | None","adapter":"treenode","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"None","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"preserve_tree_structure","result_mode":"mutated_argument","mutated_parameter":0,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"# Data structure supplied to this problem.\nclass TreeNode:\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        val: int = 0,\n        left: \"TreeNode | None\" = None,\n        right: \"TreeNode | None\" = None,\n    ):\n        self.val = val\n        self.left = left\n        self.right = right\n\n\ndef recover_bst(root: TreeNode | None) -> None:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def recover_bst(root):\n    previous = first = second = None\n    def visit(node):\n        nonlocal previous, first, second\n        if previous is not None and previous.val > node.val:\n            if first is None:\n                first = previous\n            second = node\n        previous = node\n\n    current = root\n    while current:\n        if current.left is None:\n            visit(current)\n            current = current.right\n        else:\n            predecessor = current.left\n            while predecessor.right is not None and predecessor.right is not current:\n                predecessor = predecessor.right\n            if predecessor.right is None:\n                predecessor.right = current\n                current = current.left\n            else:\n                predecessor.right = None\n                visit(current)\n                current = current.right\n    first.val, second.val = second.val, first.val\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def recover_bst(root):\n    previous = first = second = None\n    def visit(node):\n        nonlocal previous, first, second\n        if previous is not None and previous.val > node.val:\n            if first is None:\n                first = previous\n            if second is None:\n                second = node\n        previous = node\n\n    current = root\n    while current:\n        if current.left is None:\n            visit(current)\n            current = current.right\n        else:\n            predecessor = current.left\n            while predecessor.right is not None and predecessor.right is not current:\n                predecessor = predecessor.right\n            if predecessor.right is None:\n                predecessor.right = current\n                current = current.left\n            else:\n                predecessor.right = None\n                visit(current)\n                current = current.right\n    first.val, second.val = second.val, first.val\n","def recover_bst(root):\n    stack = [root]\n    while stack:\n        node = stack.pop()\n        if node.left:\n            if node.left.val > node.val:\n                node.left.val,node.val = node.val,node.left.val\n            stack.append(node.left)\n        if node.right:\n            if node.right.val < node.val:\n                node.right.val,node.val = node.val,node.right.val\n            stack.append(node.right)\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(n)","target_space_complexity":"O(1) auxiliary (Morris traversal)","estimated_minutes":35,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":2,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":1,"edge_cases":1},"hints":["An inorder traversal of a valid BST yields strictly increasing values.","Two swapped positions create one inversion if adjacent, or two inversions otherwise. Keep the earlier node of the first inversion and the later node of the last.","Traverse inorder, retaining previous. On previous.val > current.val: set first to previous if unset, and always set second to current. Swap first.val and second.val after traversal.","A stack gives a straightforward O(h)-space traversal. Morris traversal temporarily threads each left-subtree predecessor back to its parent, removes each thread on the second encounter, and uses O(1) extra space."],"editorial":"In sorted inorder order, swapping positions i < j makes the larger misplaced value the earlier endpoint of the first descending pair and the smaller misplaced value the later endpoint of the last descending pair. These may be the same pair when j = i+1. Track both endpoints while traversing the entire tree; do not repair values early. The reference uses Morris traversal: find the rightmost node of a left subtree, add a temporary link back to its parent on first encounter, and remove it before visiting that parent on the second encounter. Every temporary link is restored, then the two values are swapped. Each edge is examined a constant number of times. A conventional stack is also correct, with O(h) extra memory; recursive traversals may overflow on a deep chain.","tests":[{"id":"lc-99-1","arguments":[[1,3,null,null,2]],"expected":[3,1,null,null,2],"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Inorder values are [3,2,1], but must be [1,2,3]. Swap the values at the root and its left child; the node holding 2 stays in place.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-99-2","arguments":[[3,1,4,null,null,2]],"expected":[2,1,4,null,null,3],"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Inorder is [1,3,2,4]. Swap 3 with the deeper 2 in its right subtree. The shape stays [root, left, right, null, null, right.left].","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-99-3","arguments":[[1,2]],"expected":[2,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-99-4","arguments":[[2,null,1]],"expected":[1,null,2],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-99-5","arguments":[[4,2,6,7,3,5,1]],"expected":[4,2,6,1,3,5,7],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-99-6","arguments":[[4,6,2,1,3,5,7]],"expected":[4,2,6,1,3,5,7],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-99-7","arguments":[[3,2,6,1,4,5,7]],"expected":[4,2,6,1,3,5,7],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-99-8","arguments":[[5,2,6,1,3,4,7]],"expected":[4,2,6,1,3,5,7],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-99-9","arguments":[[1,2,6,4,3,5,7]],"expected":[4,2,6,1,3,5,7],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-99-10","arguments":[[7,2,6,1,3,5,4]],"expected":[4,2,6,1,3,5,7],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-99-11","arguments":[[4,1,null,2,null,3]],"expected":[4,3,null,2,null,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-99-12","arguments":[[1,null,4,null,3,null,2]],"expected":[1,null,2,null,3,null,4],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-99-13","arguments":[[-2147483648,2147483647]],"expected":[2147483647,-2147